From 86d78c9f875ad4687234e173f20d9b196c1d5410 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Koudai Aono <koxudaxi@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 16:40:09 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] mellum: mxfp4 moe experts

Open a Mellum file whose routed experts are all MXFP4_MOE, refuse every
mixture by name, read the expert index and the pack at the quant's own size,
and run the MoE and the layer loop with tensors staged as half. The double
reference reads MXFP4 too, so the real-weights gate compares against it.

Gates: MXFP4 config accepted, one-layer and mixed-down files refused by name;
ds4_test --mellum-moe passes on the real MXFP4 file (selection 0 differ,
weights 2.58e-07, staged reference 3.62e-05 at the worst layer); Q8 resident
medians after the loaders are 3,814 t/s prefill and 118.75 t/s decode against
3,987 and 125.08 before, inside the 10% cap; the MXFP4 same-machine pair is
4,038 / 143.39 against the d2d9338 reference's 3,996 / 143.31. Both SHA-verified
files load. Evidence in docs/reports/mellum-engine-evidence.md.

Upstream: not offered, fork only
Retire-when: upstream supports JetBrains MXFP4_MOE
Carried-commits: 0adf6bafb1f17e642124b60b183575864f118629 989dc7c8dada668500773328c00d4e851805a842 f6d49a5d57b8566809d53412ac470bd897dd811b 362dca64275b54cd9f6694441618f411fdabd1d5 24175f3845987c0761d4186ec66be7c7735a3f4b 37ccfd165c7d82afd4ef1719c5f0a1acbdac32fd fe2001bd9b3b660a7e15ebeecab2ce28e0928d2c ed405beb79cee502b1c3cf2ce28bd3657118795c 4fa5070983da883b42fc08eb0f0670f4aa4b730a d49c06cb0f999b6c780ec2bc4e3186e50cb75a65 48c5b937180bac334d80e390ebd37d550d9f08cc e2273c997bb9a1322a119c4ae0e5f25fe8d55faf a9fd4f8e2f1e5c50b847391668811380a6d653ec
